        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0607" n="581" xml:id="pg581"/>

                <head>289. Memorandum From the Under Secretary of State’s Special Assistant
                    (Sanders) to Robert L. Burns of the Executive Secretariat<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d289-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                ><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                                when="1957-11-01">November 1, 1957</date>.</hi></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Conference on the Law of the Sea</item>
                </list>
                <p>As agreed over the telephone I enclose summaries of the discussions at the
                    meeting with the Under Secretary on Monday, October 28, 1957.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d289-f2"/> The summaries have been prepared by the persons
                    participating in the discussions. I also attach a rough suggested outline
                    indicating the sequence of the discussion.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d289-f3"/> I do
                    not suggest that all the material offered by the participants be included in
                    your summary.</p>
                <p>[Here follows a suggested distribution list.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">WS</hi></signed></closer>





                <xi:include href="d289-a1.xml" xpointer="d289-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d289-a2.xml" xpointer="d289-a2"/>
                <xi:include href="d289-a3.xml" xpointer="d289-a3"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d289-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d289-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 399.731/11–157. Confidential.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d289-f2" n="2" xml:id="d289-f2-content">
                <p>A memorandum of October 23 by Robert A. McKinnon of the Executive Secretariat
                    reported that at the meeting on October 28, Admiral Chester Ward, Judge Advocate
                    General of the Navy, and Captain William Hearn of his office, would represent
                    the Department of Defense; and Ross Leffler, Assistant Secretary for Fisheries
                    and Wildlife, and William M. Terry of his office, would represent the Department
                    of the Interior. McKinnon’s memorandum also indicated that Sanders, Herrington,
                    and Becker were to be participants for the Department of State, and that Murphy
                    was invited but unable to attend. (<hi rendition="#italic">Ibid.,</hi>
                    399.731/10–2157)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d289-f3" n="3" xml:id="d289-f3-content">
                <p>The outline is Annex A, and the summaries are Annexes B, C, and D. Annex B is not
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
